_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: v4.5.2.stable.official [6ce3de25a], v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8183) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600H with Radeon Graphics (12 threads) - 15.34 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen selecting multiple instanced nodes and resetting a resource, the resource is getting removed instead of resetting to the default from the instanced scene.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d6c1d06-1424-4e64-b741-eeac8671cd3e\n\nThis really makes an impact on usability when working with modular models. The temporary fix is to click on every node in the scene tree and reset the resource one node at a time.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a scene.\n2. Instantiate that scene multiple times in an another scene.\n3. Change some default resources on the instanced scene nodes.\n4. Try resetting that resource when multiple nodes are selected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[node_multiselect_difference_2026-03-23_22-27-37.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26193498/node_multiselect_difference_2026-03-23_22-27-37.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url"